  "reviewer_notes": "This paper is an energy audit of two Colombian lime factories using ISO-13579 energy/mass balances. Two applications (Factory 1, Factory 2) were coded, each with an energy-balance efficiency model (M1/M3) and an energy-intensity ratio model (M2/M4). The models are deterministic physical balances (not statistical fits), so estimation, variable selection, fit and validation metrics are largely not applicable; efficiency and intensity outputs are recorded in model_parameters_reported and (for the savings potential) energy_result. Control volume = the limekiln (unit). No model-specific limitations (mechanisms), study limitations, implementation barriers, or model adaptations were stated in the text (the proposed twin-shaft-regenerative kiln upgrade is a process/technology change, not a model adaptation).",
